{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeRCSWKpuzRyYZutyiTKu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The health-route test fails because of a bug in `router/routes.go`, not in `routes/public.map`.\n\n**Cause:** `HealthHandler()` is hardcoded to return `\"wildcard\"` instead of `\"health\"`:\n\n```go\nfunc HealthHandler() string { return \"wildcard\" }\n```\n\nThe map file (`routes/public.map`) is correct — it lists `/health` mapped to `health` before the `/*` wildcard entry, so routing precedence isn't the problem. The failure is purely a source-level bug: the handler function's return value doesn't reflect the matched route name (`health`) and instead always returns the wildcard's value (`wildcard`), causing `TestHealthRoute` to fail with \"shadowed by wildcard\".\n\n**Fix (without touching routes/public.map):** update `router/routes.go` so `HealthHandler()` returns `\"health\"` (e.g., have it look up/return the route name it was matched against, rather than a hardcoded `\"wildcard\"` string)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":673,"cache_read_input_tokens":2225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":673},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e74e620c-a430-476c-bc15-4c7acfa378eb","uuid":"f225ef0f-ccf8-44a3-a7a8-810299806a9f","timestamp":"2026-08-26T10:25:16.797Z","request_id":"req_011CeRCSVYx37TxYy9CFnH63"}
